Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.04,0:00:01.74,Default,,0,0,0,,While I sort these loose screws,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.74,0:00:03.86,Default,,0,0,0,,one question keeps snagging me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.18,0:00:07.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Why does Pandora's box mean\Ndisaster?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.86,0:00:10.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I reach for the answer and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.12,0:00:11.26,Default,,0,0,0,,the old story opens.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.74,0:00:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Pandora is given a sealed\Ncontainer
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.52,0:00:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,and warned not to open it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.32,0:00:18.72,Default,,0,0,0,,In the oldest Greek telling, it
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.72,0:00:21.12,Default,,0,0,0,,is actually a jar, not a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.12,0:00:21.58,Default,,0,0,0,,box.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.76,0:00:24.44,Default,,0,0,0,,That warning turns the container\Ninto
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.44,0:00:26.56,Default,,0,0,0,,a mystery sitting within reach.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.64,0:00:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,curiosity keeps pressing until\Npandora finally
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.40,0:00:32.56,Default,,0,0,0,,lifts the lid then the trouble
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.56,0:00:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,is suddenly bigger than the choice
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.98,0:00:37.18,Default,,0,0,0,,that released it evils and\Nhardships
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.18,0:00:39.58,Default,,0,0,0,,rush into the world before she
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.58,0:00:42.62,Default,,0,0,0,,can contain them pandora shuts the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.62,0:00:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,container but what escaped cannot\Nsimply
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.82,0:00:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,be called back only hope remains
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.84,0:00:50.84,Default,,0,0,0,,inside that strange ending keeps\Nthe
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.84,0:00:52.30,Default,,0,0,0,,myth from being just a warning
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.30,0:00:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,about curiosity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.58,0:00:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The story is really about\Nconsequences
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.92,0:00:58.84,Default,,0,0,0,,that can outrun the action that
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.84,0:00:59.62,Default,,0,0,0,,starts them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.60,0:01:02.70,Default,,0,0,0,,One small decision can release\Nproblems
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.70,0:01:04.74,Default,,0,0,0,,far larger than the decision\Nitself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.88,0:01:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,That is why we still talk
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.06,0:01:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,about opening Pandora's box.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.94,0:01:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,We mean a choice may trigger
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.38,0:01:12.64,Default,,0,0,0,,a chain of trouble that keeps
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.64,0:01:13.38,Default,,0,0,0,,spreading.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.38,0:01:15.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The danger is not that every
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.72,0:01:18.84,Default,,0,0,0,,forbidden thing must stay\Nuntouched forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.84,0:01:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,It is that some doors are
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.62,0:01:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,much easier to open than to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.22,0:01:22.88,Default,,0,0,0,,close.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.88,0:01:26.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes the smallest opening\Nchanges everything
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.60,0:01:27.64,Default,,0,0,0,,that follows.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.64,0:01:28.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Like and subscribe to grow more
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.72,0:01:29.44,Default,,0,0,0,,questions.
